{
  "summary": "Disables peer announcement of periodic wallet transaction resubmissions when `-privatebroadcast` is enabled. Unconfirmed wallet transactions are still resubmitted to the local mempool, but `node::TxBroadcast::MEMPOOL_NO_BROADCAST` is used instead of broadcasting to all peers.",
  "problem": "Periodic wallet rebroadcasts announce unconfirmed transactions over standard P2P clearnet connections. For users relying on `-privatebroadcast` to conceal transaction origins, periodic resubmission (or rebroadcasts triggered by events like incoming payments) deanonymizes the node as the wallet owner.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'for users opting into private broadcast, it seems a bridge too far for them to expect the current behavior. e.g. an incoming dust payment triggering your node to rebroadcast 24-36th later over clearnet'",
    "Release notes: 'A transaction that was broadcast privately and later received back from the network was otherwise announced again from the node's own connections, which revealed its origin.'"
  ],
